  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[4]{3x+1} & =-10 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{3x+1} & =2 \\\\ (\\sqrt[4]{3x+1})^{4} & ={2}^{4} \\\\ 3x+1 & =16 \\\\ 3x & =15 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sqrt[4]{3\\cdot 5+1}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\sqrt[4]{16}+10 & =0 \\\\ -5\\cdot 2+10 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=5.$",
